1
00:00:00,169 --> 00:00:04,609
Two hundred people. One field. — And a record for every one of them.

2
00:00:08,072 --> 00:00:13,324
Camps are planned here, alongside the clinic that staffs them.

3
00:00:13,324 --> 00:00:20,015
Services, people, stations and supplies — the four things a camp needs.

4
00:00:20,015 --> 00:00:24,842
A camp takes clinicians out of the building.

5
00:00:24,842 --> 00:00:28,853
Pick one who is already booked, and the clinic says so first.

6
00:00:28,853 --> 00:00:35,280
Three appointments inside the camp window, listed before anyone is rostered.

7
00:00:35,280 --> 00:00:40,282
At the gate, a walk-in with no appointment and no file.

8
00:00:40,282 --> 00:00:46,494
Name, age, consent. Nothing that slows the queue down.

9
00:00:46,494 --> 00:00:51,880
A token for them, and a record for you — at the point of contact.

10
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:55,787
Every station, live, with the longest wait at each.

11
00:00:55,787 --> 00:01:02,588
Fourteen waiting at the doctor, thirty-six minutes deep. That is where to move people.

12
00:01:02,588 --> 00:01:06,586
Ninety-four seen. Thirty-seven now have a patient record.

13
00:01:06,586 --> 00:01:14,791
Twenty-one booked a follow-up — the number that decides whether the camp pays for itself.

14
00:01:14,791 --> 00:01:18,303
The sponsor funded it, so the sponsor gets counts.

15
00:01:18,303 --> 00:01:23,953
No names, no dates of birth, and small groups combined so nobody is identifiable.

16
00:01:24,143 --> 00:01:27,943
A clinic that moved. — Not a clipboard you type up later.
